if {game_state} == 2.0:
	if {dialogue} == 0.0:
		Faunus: Ah! Check out the crocus blossom
		Faunus: Interacting with a flower directly will tell you what it needs
		Faunus: Explore the map little one, but remember
		Faunus: not every problem will come with a solution that’s immediately apparent
		Faunus: Stay alert and curious, little one, and I am sure you will find every solution that you need
		set {dialogue} = 1.0
	elif {dialogue} == 1.0:
		Faunus: Looks like the bear is deep in hibernation and blocking the sun
		Faunus: Have you tried looking around to find them something to eat?
		Faunus: Bears get very hungry and lethargic in their hibernation
		Faunus: It might help if you look around for something they’d enjoy eating
		Faunus: That ought to wake em up
elif {game_state} == 3.0:
	Faunus: Nesting material huh?
	Faunus: If you explore the map and keep a keen eye out
	Faunus: you’re sure to find everything you need in due time
	Faunus: Chin up little one
	Faunus: I know you’re up for the task
elif {game_state} == 4.0:
	Faunus: Put the berries close to the bear and hope they aren't too groggy.
	Faunus: I'm sure they'll find somewhere else to go
elif {game_state} == 5.0:
	if {went_and_returned} == 0.0:
		This flower has more than enough sunlight now
		However, it still doesn’t seem ready to wake up
		Faunus: Seems like the flower is a bit more demanding than we might have hoped
		Faunus: From my experience I think a little musical performance might be just what this flower needs to fully waken
		Faunus: What a gift and delight music is!
		Faunus: Of course, you will need an instrument first
		Faunus: Lucky for you little one, I can make any instrument with the right materials
		Faunus: How about a fiddle?
		Faunus: I believe it would suit you quite well
		Faunus: Yes, yes! It would suit you perfectly indeed!
		You: I’m not so sure…
		You: I don’t want to let the forest down
		You: but I wouldn’t exactly call myself much of a musician
		Faunus: on’t you worry about that, little one
		Faunus: You have done so well in your duties and been so brave
		Faunus: Don’t lose faith in yourself now!
		Faunus: Just let the spirit of spring flow through you
		Faunus: and I am confident you will give a performance for the ages
		Faunus: Just don't give up hope
		Faunus: All you need to do is find a suitable piece of carving wood
		Faunus: and something to use for the strings while I collect my carving knife
		Faunus: I see a new area of the forest has opened now that the bear has awoken from its slumber
		Faunus: Why don’t you try looking out there?
		Faunus: The forest provides for those who have provided for it, don't you know?
		Faunus: I will see you again very soon, little one
		Faunus: Keep your spirit as unwavering and pure
		as it has remained throughout all of your duties I know you cannot help but do
		Faunus: You have nothing to fear
		Faunus: See you soon!
		[signal arg="leaving"]
	if {went_and_returned} == 1.0:
		Faunus: You did well, little one! And what are these?
		Faunus: Strands of Amalthea’s hair?
		Faunus: To have even her blessing like this…
		Faunus: You truly are exactly who I hoped you would be
		Faunus: Don’t worry about your playing ability
		Faunus: It is carved even in the bedrock below this forest that you have always been meant to play this tune and awaken this springtime
		Faunus: However…
		Faunus: I seem to have misplaced my carving knife
		Faunus: I could have sworn it was by the shack, but I cannot find it anywhere
		Faunus: Maybe it’s my old age
		Faunus: My memory is not what it used to be
		Faunus: but I still cannot believe I have become so forgetful…
		Faunus: I was supposed to have at least a bit more time than this to keep such faculties…
		Faunus: it’s hard to accept…
		You: Wait a second, Faunus sir
		You: I know someone with an eye for shiny things
		You: Maybe he knows where your carving knife could be
		Faunus: In that case, please dear one, could you go try to fetch it for me?
		Faunus: I know it’s one more task you did not ask for, but that is the forest for you
		Faunus: always evading predicability and scoffing at the timing of lesser creatures’ plans
		Faunus: ~heh heh~
		Faunus: Beautiful isn’t it?
		set {game_state} = 6.0
elif {game_state} == 6.0:
	if {has_knife} == 0.0:
		Faunus can’t make anything out of the collected materials until he has his carving knife
		Better go find Mr. Crow
	elif {has_knife} == 1.0:
		Faunus: Thank you so much dear one for returning my carving knife to me
		Faunus: That bird loves to act the trickster
		Faunus: You think he would be a bit nicer to an old goat
		Faunus: but his nature is his nature
		Faunus: I cannot fault him for this any more than I could fault that of any of us belonging to the forest
		You: I had to promise he’d get it back
		You: You might have to bargain with him for it later…
		You: And he wants to watch as well
		You: He said something strange about wanting to see if I’m truly what you’ve been looking for
		Faunus: ~heh heh~ Of course he did
		Faunus: Saying such things is in his nature
		Faunus: It is a blessing to live long enough to know the hearts of old friends so thoroughly
		Faunus: Ah well, I should start building you your fiddle before I get too lost in my memories
		Faunus: Go on and fetch everyone to enjoy your performance and witness the true awakening of spring
		Faunus: It won’t take me long to carve this instrument to resonate with the purity and simplicity curled up inside your heart ready to sprout
		We’re almost there, brave one
		[signal arg="take fiddle materials"]
		set {game_state} = 7.0
elif {game_state} == 7.0:
	if {crow_invited}  ==  1.0 and {seelie_invited}  ==  1.0 and {unicorn_invited}  ==  1.0:
		Faunus: Wonderful job gathering everyone for the performance, little one
		Faunus: Everyone’s here and with perfect timing too! I just finished constructing the fiddle for you to play
		Faunus: All that’s left now is for you to play it, awaken the crocus and springtime with it
		Faunus: After seeing how well you have done in all of your duties so far brave one
		Faunus: I have full faith you will complete your final task with perfect gravitas
		Faunus: Spring is counting on you, little one
		Faunus: You need not worry you will let it down now
		Faunus: Now go on to the flower and play for it
		Faunus: Coming from your heart, it will not fail
		Obtained the Fiddle
		[signal arg="give fiddle"]
		[signal arg="party"]
		Faunus: It is time now, I'll follow your lead
		audio music -
		[wait time="5.0"]
		audio music "res://audio/music/Dance! (Game Jam).wav"
		[signal arg="dance"]
		Faunus: dance everyone
		set {game_state} = 8.0
		[signal arg="dance end"]
	else:
		Faunus seems to be completely engrossed in his craft
		You’d best focus on collecting the forest inhabitants right now
elif {game_state} == 8.0:
	if {thanks_done} == 0.0:
		Faunus: Congratulations, brave one! You performed your duties perfectly
		Faunus: Springtime has come, and it’s all thanks to your hard work and dedication
		You: Thank you, sir. I’m glad to have not let the forest down
		Faunus: Do you still have some something to discuss with the others or could I talk to you somewhere quiet?
		set {thanks_done} = 1.0
		- yes
			set {game_state} = 9.0
			[signal arg="finale"]
		- no
			Faun: I'll wait
	Faun: can i talk to you now?
	- yes
		set {game_state} = 9.0
		[signal arg="finale"]
	- no
		Faun: I'll wait
elif {game_state} == 9.0:
	Faunus: Thank you for lending me your time, when you should be celebrating
	Faunus: Know I wouldn't keep you if it was not important
	You: Of course not, so what is it you wanted to talk about sir?
	Faunus: The spirit of the forest runs through your veins just as much as it does mine, little one
	Faunus: For a lost founding kept in slumber for so long
	Faunus: it’s clear that you are the successor the forest has chosen for me
	Faunus: after all this time I’ve been waiting and searching
	You: Hold on, your successor?
	Faunus: promised you at the beginning that I would reveal all in due time
	Faunus: and that time has come
	Faunus: You see, I am quite old
	Faunus: Of course, I still have a couple hundred years left to perform my duties as the guardian of the forest
	Faunus: before I fully return to the essence of the forest
	Faunus: but as you can see, I need assistance performing my duties…
	Faunus: and more importantly, I need a successor to take on as an apprentice
	Faunus: as it is no quick feat to learn how to be a proper steward of this land
	You: You truly want me to become your apprentice and the next guardian, sir?
	You: But I’m just a mortal who cannot even remember their own name
	You: How could I possibly ever take your place?
	Faunus: Ah yes… perhaps once you were simply a mortal
	Faunus: but your long hibernation slumbering in this forest
	Faunus: like a bulb that takes time to sprout out shoots and blooms has transformed you into something greater
	Faunus: Perhaps this was always your destiny
	Faunus: Amalthea’s presence and blessing is not one bestowed to just anyone
	Faunus: In any case, it’s for the best your true name evades your recollection in any case for your safety in fae dealings
	Faunus: However, like the rest of us in this forest, I think it may be time for you to come up with your own chosen name to go by, little one
	Faunus: Your base mortal nature makes you empathetic to all the creatures of the forest in a way most born here are not
	Faunus: but your lifespan is no longer as brief a flicker as that of a true mortal
	Faunus: and neither is the spirit beating and swirling inside of you
	You: …
	You: I don’t think I can do this without you, Faunus sir
	You: How could I ever be so worthy?
	Faunus: Do not worry brave one!
	Faunus: As I said, there is still proper time left for me to mentor you bit by bit
	Faunus: These duties will not fall on you all at once
	Faunus: I simply have one question for you
	Faunus: do you love this forest truly in all of its complexities?
	You: I do
	You: After performing my spring awakening duties and becoming familiar with all the flora of this forest as well as its inhabitants
	You: It has become dear to me
	Faunus: You see now, brave one?
	Faunus: It was always meant to be you
	Faunus: This is your calling, duty and pleasure
	Faunus: Your worthiness shines so brightly
	Faunus: it is clear you are the only one meant to be the next guardian
	Faunus: Do not doubt your capabilities!
	You: If it is you sir who says so, who am I to question myself for this role?
	You: I will not let you or this forest down
	You: I accept all you say
	You: I will be your apprentice, and in time, the next guardian of the forest
	Faunus: That’s a good one
	Faunus: My brave one
	Faunus: My apprentice and my successor
	You: But what will happen to you when your time ends?
	Faunus: I will simply return back to nature
	Faunus: My presence will always linger in this forest and will always protect you
	Faunus: I wonder what leafy form my essence will take
	Faunus: Whatever the forest deems proper, I will be happy with, as it is right
	Faunus: However, I think I would like to take the form of an oak tree if the forest takes such wishes as this into account
	Faunus: It is not a sad thing but one that is beautiful
	Faunus: You will come to take this fully to heart in time, dear one
	You: I don’t understand all of this right now, but I believe you, Faunus sir
	You: Even with this small duty and even when I doubted myself
	You: You led me well and did not share such doubts in me
	You: I am ready to follow your mentoring and instruction wherever it goes
	Faunus: Excellent! Believe me, brave one, you contain so much more power than you believe
	Faunus: Come now\: let us enjoy the festivities and the fruits of your labour a while longer
	Faunus: Tomorrow is another day, and your further instruction under me can wait to continue then
	Faunus: Let us play our melodies and continue the dance and reveleries a while longer
	Faunus: You deserve this celebration, future guardian of the forest
	[signal arg="end"]